  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mapping of potential skills development projects in Namibia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The combi-track &quot;Green Hydrogen&quot; (GH2) aims to catalyse the development of GH2 economies in Namibia and South Africa. On GH2 several studies have been executed, including on Dutch propositions for South Africa and Namibia. For both propositions, skills development has been identified as areas for cooperation. This study is a follow-up of this identification.The Netherlands government, in collaboration with private sector stakeholders, aims to explore and promote GH2 initiatives in Namibia. Namibia has the ambition to develop GH2, for export purposes as well as local use and to phase out the use of fossil energy. GH2 holds significant potential for sustainable energy production and the energy transition. Besides, it will contribute to green economic development and the creation of green jobs in Namibia.Currently, there is a lack of skilled people that are needed to develop potential GH2 projects in collaboration with Dutch stakeholders, and that match with Dutch technologies and innovations.This study aims to know the main stakeholders in the Netherlands and Namibia, active or that could potentially be active in skills development related to GH2, to understand concrete opportunities and leads for bilateral cooperation in skills development.Furthermore, this study aims to identify the three most promising leads for bilateral projects between the Netherlands and Namibia in the field of skills development.</narrative>
  </description>
